  "step_3": "The decision reason emphasizes comparing probabilities of favorable outcomes and preferring the lottery with the higher probability of such an outcome. In Step 1, we determined that defining 'favorable outcome' as 0 EUR or better makes Lottery A superior in probability (50% vs 0%), and the reason would prefer A. In Step 2, we saw that the individual explicitly values the 50% chance of losing nothing (0 EUR) and rejects the certainty of loss in B. They focus on the probabilistic advantage of avoiding loss, which aligns with the core logic of the decision reason. While the individual also mentions psychological aspects (easier to take risk when some money remains), the central justification is the preference for a non-zero chance of no loss over certain loss—this directly reflects a comparison of probabilities of favorable outcomes. The information considered (probabilities of no loss) and the justification (preferring a chance of no loss over certain loss) match the rule of the decision reason. Therefore, it is highly likely the individual used this reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 95
}

{
